/* =============================================================================
   DIAGNOSTIC: find out which column name Power Fx cannot resolve
   Read-only. Nothing here writes to Dataverse.

   WHY: "Name isn't valid" points at the member access, not at the cause. The
   squiggle lands on `.SubmittedOn` whether the real problem is the column, the
   table it is on, the filter in front of it, or a stale data source. These
   probes separate those cases, because each one fails independently.

   HOW: insert a blank Label on a scratch screen and paste ONE probe at a time
   into its Text property. A probe that shows a number or a date resolves; one
   that goes red is your answer. Do not chain them with & - a single failure
   would take the whole line down and you would learn nothing.
   ============================================================================ */


/* ---- PROBE 1: does the table itself resolve? ---------------------------- */
CountRows('RolePreference PreferenceResponses')

/* ---- PROBE 2: does EmployeeID resolve on THAT table? -------------------- */
CountRows(Filter('RolePreference PreferenceResponses', EmployeeID = varUser.EmpId))

/* ---- PROBE 3: does Stage2Status resolve, AND is it Text? ----------------
   Red here with probes 1-2 green means Stage2Status exists but is a CHOICE,
   not Text. Comparing a choice to the string "Submitted" is a type error, and
   Power Fx then cannot type the LookUp's result - so the squiggle appears
   downstream, on .SubmittedOn, and the real fault is here. The app wants Text
   for Stage1Status and Stage2Status; see docs/dataverse-setup.md. */
CountRows(Filter('RolePreference PreferenceResponses', Stage2Status = "Submitted"))

/* ---- PROBE 4: does SubmittedOn resolve on PreferenceResponses? ----------
   No filter at all, so this isolates the column from everything else. */
Text(First('RolePreference PreferenceResponses').SubmittedOn, "dd/mm/yyyy")

/* ---- PROBE 5: the same column on the OTHER table ------------------------
   'RolePreference Preferences' ALSO has a SubmittedOn, and it is the one the
   ranking uses. If probe 5 is green and probe 4 is red, the column was added
   to Preferences rather than to PreferenceResponses - an easy mistake, because
   checking "is SubmittedOn there?" finds it either way. */
Text(First('RolePreference Preferences').SubmittedOn, "dd/mm/yyyy")

/* ---- PROBE 6: is the display name what you think it is? -----------------
   A column created as "Submitted On" has a SPACE in its display name, and
   Power Fx then needs single quotes around it. If this one is green while
   probe 4 is red, that is the whole problem - either rename the column to
   SubmittedOn in make.powerapps.com, or quote it everywhere in the app. */
Text(First('RolePreference PreferenceResponses').'Submitted On', "dd/mm/yyyy")

/* ---- PROBE 7: list the columns the app can actually see -----------------
   Paste into a blank Gallery's Items instead of a Label. It renders one row
   per record with the four fields OnStart needs; a column missing from the
   data source cannot be selected in the gallery's field picker, which is a
   quick visual confirmation of what Studio believes the schema is. */
FirstN(
    ForAll(
        'RolePreference PreferenceResponses' As r,
        {Emp: r.EmployeeID, Role: r.RoleKey, Stage2: r.Stage2Status, When: r.SubmittedOn}
    ),
    5
)


/* =============================================================================
   READING THE RESULT

   All green .................. the schema is fine; the error you are looking at
                                is stale. Close and reopen the app in Studio -
                                it caches the binding, and a refresh of one data
                                source does not re-resolve the others.
   1 red ...................... the data source is not added, or points at a
                                different environment.
   2 red ...................... EmployeeID is missing or is not Text.
   3 red ...................... Stage2Status is a Choice; make it Text.
   4 red, 5 green ............. SubmittedOn is on Preferences, not on
                                PreferenceResponses. Add it to the latter.
   4 red, 6 green ............. the display name has a space in it.
   4 red, 5 and 6 red ......... the column genuinely is not on that table, or
                                the data source has not been refreshed since it
                                was added. Data -> the table -> ... -> Refresh,
                                then reopen the app.

   REFRESHING ONE TABLE DOES NOT REFRESH THE OTHERS. Renaming a column on
   Alignments and refreshing Alignments leaves PreferenceResponses bound to
   whatever Studio cached earlier. Refresh every table you have edited.
   ============================================================================ */
